'''Carpinchera''' ({{Literal translation|place of {{W|capybara}}}}; {{Langx|awt|Tapỹi-Kapi'iwa}}) is a [[regions of Balisca|region]] in southwestern [[Bayara]], within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. It borders [[Xaraba]] to the north and northwest, [[Camaca]] to the south and southwest, and bounded by the [[Salsipuedes Sea]] to the west. It has an area of {{convert|64007.44|km2|abbr=on}} making it one of the smallest regions in Balisca. According to the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]] it is the second most populous region, with a recorded population of 14,783,470. The administrative capital and most populous city is [[Macaio]].

The region's climate is {{W|tropical climate|tropical}} along the coast, with dry winters and extremely rainy summers.

